cache:query:what is the story of cain
$641
Cain was the first son of Adam and Eve (Genesis 4:1) and worked as a husbandman, while his brother Abel was a shepherd (chunk‑41).  Out of jealousy he killed Abel, and when God asked him “Where is thy brother Abel?” Cain replied, “I know not; am I my brother’s keeper?” God then said that the blood of Abel cried out from the earth and pronounced a curse on Cain, condemning him to be a fugitive on the earth (chunk‑45).  After this, Cain left the presence of the Lord, settled as a wanderer on the east side of Eden, took a wife, and they bore a son named Henoch; Cain built a city and named it after his son (chunk‑49).
$4
