cache:query:What happened in chapter 3?
$843
Chapter 3 describes the temptation, the fall, and the immediate aftermath.  
- God had warned that the fruit of the tree in the middle of Paradise should not be eaten or touched, lest one die; the serpent contradicted this, telling the woman she would not die and that eating would open her eyes and make her “as Gods” (knowing good and evil)【chunk-29】.  
- The woman saw the tree’s fruit was pleasing and ate it, gave some to her husband, and he also ate. Their eyes were opened, they realized they were naked, and they sewed fig leaves together to make aprons【chunk-30】.  
- Hearing the Lord God walking in Paradise, Adam and his wife hid among the trees. The Lord called to Adam, asking “Where art thou?” Adam replied that he heard God’s voice, was afraid because he was naked, and therefore hid himself【chunk-33】.
$4
